{title: He Hideth My Soul}
{artist: Fanny Crosby & William Kirkpatrick}
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 80}

Verse 1
A [Bb]wonderful Savior is [Eb]Jesus my [Bb]Lord, a wonderful Savior to [F]me:
he [Bb]hideth my soul in the [Eb]cleft of the [Bb]rock, where [Eb]rivers of [F]pleasure I [Bb]see.

Chorus
He [Bb]hideth my soul in the [Eb]cleft of the [Bb]rock that [Bb]shadows a dry, thirsty [F]land;
he [Bb]hideth my life in the [Eb]depths of his [Bb]love, and [Eb]covers me [F]there with his [Bb]hand.
